The `navigator.onLine` check returns false positives in browsers - it only indicates network interface status, not actual internet connectivity. A device can have `navigator.onLine === true` but still lack internet access (e.g., connected to a router with no WAN connection). This makes `ERR_NO_INTERNET` unreliable for browser environments.
